  "description": "HyperSL is a spectral foundation model for hyperspectral image interpretation. It standardizes spectral vectors into a common token format, embeds wavelength information into position encoding, and is pretrained on over 300 million spectral instances from diverse global sources. HyperSL achieves state-of-the-art performance in classification and change detection tasks, with strong cross-sensor and cross-domain generalization.",
